Trust: Q1, Q2 to the digits shown (grid-converged). Q3: local searches from 5-8 starts each, mass cap active in every good one; the best (a) values scatter 0.083-0.105%, so (a) is NOT converged and a lower miss surely exists; (b) scatters only 0.984-0.994%, somewhat better trusted, still an upper bound only.

ADDENDUM, written AFTER reading the README (not blind): in Q2 I read "9.77 times the bare skin's mass per area" as the load a = 9.77
(density 10.77 inside 0.4). The author's disc has density 9.77 (a = 8.77). With a = 8.77 my solver gives (verify.out): w11 1.94929,
B 0.8390, places 1.0326 (vacuum), 1.1449 (reference), 1.0926 (doubled), 1.2320 (halved), tube 1.1338. The blind figures above stand as
my answer to the question as I first read it.
